RuboCop 1.89.0 whitequark EOF reporting ranges
============================================

Upstream: https://github.com/rubocop/rubocop
License: MIT; full text in licenses/RUBOCOP.txt.
Issue: https://github.com/owayo/sonicop/issues/175

Recorded with MRI 4.0.7 (x64-mingw-ucrt), RuboCop 1.89.0,
parser 3.3.12.0, rubocop-ast 1.50.0, Prism 1.8.1 (CEXT), Rainbow 3.1.1.
The 18 cells use six literal byte inputs, targets 3.3/whitequark,
3.4/whitequark and 3.3/Prism. No source was evaluated by the Ruby VM.

Each offense/file record comes from actual specification JSON. The existing
five-byte no-LF input was reused from three completed 55-file batches. Five
additional LF/CRLF/UTF8-prefix/valid-hex controls were recorded in one five-file
batch per setting. The new three batches completed all inputs and preserved
input bytes/mode/mtime. ENV4 was removed from a child environment copy and
actual loaded versions/effective target/backend were retained privately.
Native output was never used to construct expectations.

The fixture combines exact per-file reference records, not a newly captured
six-file report: only the known no-LF path was projected to the declared case
path; all offense fields are unchanged. Group summary counts are derived from
the six authoritative records. Runtime metadata is identical across the joined
records. CLI assertions exclude only the four documented implementation runtime
identity keys; rubocop_version/ruby_patchlevel and all other JSON fields stay
strict. The capture order remains in files; duplicate diagnostics are retained.

The original stdout/stderr/argv/runtime records remain in the maintainer's
private evidence packet. Reference stderr includes the existing pending notice;
this location regression compares JSON, not the separately tracked transport
or pending-notice behavior. The public fixture contains no private cwd/path.

Regeneration inputs are source_hex and each group's YAML. Run RuboCop 1.89.0
with --config CONFIG --cache false --only Lint/Syntax --format json and the
listed paths, then compare exact per-file records. No dedicated public collector
is claimed. JSON container uses LF; source CRLF bytes remain escaped as hex.
These are diagnostics only, not correction/VM/latest/corpus/FINAL evidence.
